//? Title: Native NYSIIS: observable rewrite keys
//? Subtitle: Actual prefix/token decisions, original surname comparisons and explicit variant behavior
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Produce the library’s variable-length NYSIIS-style byte key and inspect the
actual decisions that create it. The original six examples and32-surname
comparison are retained through canonical helpers. Owned traces make
prefix/suffix rewriting, whole-token suppression and cleanup visible, while the
report distinguishes descriptive collision counts from phonetic accuracy or
identity ground truth.
)

\toc

> Specify the native rule variant before comparing keys

The producer uppercases bytes with the current C locale, rewrites prefixes and
suffixes, retains the first rewritten byte as the initial key, processes
interior tokens and applies three cleanup rules. Prefixes are
MAC→MCC,KN→N,K→C,PH/PF→FF and SCH→SSS. Suffixes IE/EE becomeY, while
DT/RT/RD/NT/ND becomeD. Interior branches include EV→AF,
vowels→A,Q→G,Z→S,M→N,KN→N,K→C,SCH→SS,PH→F and context-dependent H/W folding.

These are the actual native rules, which are preserved during conversion. A
whole token is suppressed only when its last byte equals the current key’s last
byte. Internal multi-byte replacements are not compressed character by
character, and H/W rules consult predecessor bytes in the rewritten input rather
than a separately normalized key. Consequently this implementation can differ
from other NYSIIS variants. It does not truncate to six characters, filter
nonletters or normalize Unicode. Punctuation, NUL and high bytes may survive, so
even an “alphabetic” output guarantee would be too strong for arbitrary input.

> A hand-checkable MAC trace

Prefix MAC becomesMCC. The first rewritten byteM starts the key; the firstC
appends and the secondC token is suppressed. No cleanup rule then changesMC. The
diagram uses actual prefix, first-byte and final states, and the table shows
every actual decision—including unchanged stages—rather than a report-side
encoder.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nysiis_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nysiis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::nysiis_trace("MAC");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("rewrite", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual prefix state\n{}", t.steps[0].after));
    d.node("first", {7, 0},
           std::format("Actual initial key\n{}", t.steps[2].after));
    d.node("final", {14, 0}, std::format("Actual final key\n{}", t.analysis.key));
    d.edge("rewrite", "first").edge("first", "final");
    std::print("| actual stage | actual rule | before | replacement token | appended | after |\n| --- | --- " "| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | `{}` | `{}` | {} | `{}` |\n", s.stage, s.rule,
                   s.before.empty() ? "(empty)" : s.before,
                   s.token.empty() ? "(empty)" : s.token, s.appended,
                   s.after.empty() ? "(empty)" : s.after);
    d.save_svg("build/nysiis_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual stage | actual rule | before | replacement token | appended | after |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| prefix | MAC | `MAC` | `MCC` | false | `MCC` |
| suffix | none | `MCC` | `(empty)` | false | `MCC` |
| first | first-byte | `(empty)` | `M` | true | `M` |
| interior | literal | `M` | `C` | true | `MC` |
| interior | literal | `MC` | `C` | false | `MC` |
| cleanup | none | `MC` | `(empty)` | false | `MC` |
| cleanup | none | `MC` | `(empty)` | false | `MC` |
| cleanup | none | `MC` | `(empty)` | false | `MC` |
\image(figures/nysiis_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual prefix, first-byte and final states for MAC, with all native decisions printed.)
\alttext(The duplicateC token is suppressed as a whole; empty tokens and unchanged cleanup stages remain explicit in the table.)

> Retain the original six displayed surnames

MacDonald,Catherine,Ashcraft,Ashcroft,Mueller andMiller retain their original
spellings and order. The native comparison helper calls the current canonical
Soundex and NYSIIS producers; the table displays their actual keys. The figure
shows actual NYSIIS key lengths, making variable-length output concrete without
assuming that a longer key is more accurate.

Equal keys are candidates for a broader matching process, not proof of equal
pronunciation or identity. Distinct keys likewise do not prove that names should
remain separate. The original examples of merged spellings therefore remain
observations rather than labeled successes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nysiis_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nysiis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto c =
        dm::algorithms::nysiis_compare_names(dm::algorithms::nysiis_demo_examples());
    std::vector<double> lengths;
    std::print("| original name | actual Soundex | actual native NYSIIS | NYSIIS bytes |\n| --- | --- | --- " "| ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < c.names.size(); ++i) {
        lengths.push_back(c.nysiis_keys[i].size());
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | `{}` | {} |\n", c.names[i], c.soundex_keys[i],
                   c.nysiis_keys[i], c.nysiis_keys[i].size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(lengths, c.names, "actual key bytes");
    p.size(1200, 600).title("Original six examples: actual native NYSIIS key lengths").x_label("original surname").y_label("untruncated key bytes").save_svg("build/nysiis_original.svg");
}
```
