> Retain all32 names and describe the observed grouping

The original illustrative cohort contains32 surnames, from Anderson through
Robinson. Every name and both actual keys are printed below. Distinct-key counts
describe how many groups the selected list produces. Equal-code pair counts sum
the number of unordered row pairs in each group; they are not counts of false
matches without external labels. Repeating an input row would legitimately add
another row pair, so the cohort’s identity and weighting matter.

More distinct keys on this selected list can reflect fewer merges, more splits,
or both. The original conclusion that a taller bar establishes fewer
unrelated-name errors or preserved true homophones does not follow from these
unlabeled data. The old abstract’s character-for-character Jellyfish validation
on a 4,000-word corpus was also not performed by its report program; no such
conformance claim is carried forward.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nysiis_cohort.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nysiis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto c =
        dm::algorithms::nysiis_compare_names(dm::algorithms::nysiis_demo_names());
    std::print("| original cohort name | actual Soundex | actual native NYSIIS |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < c.names.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | `{}` |\n", c.names[i], c.soundex_keys[i],
                   c.nysiis_keys[i]);
    std::print("\n| encoder | actual distinct keys | actual equal-code unordered row pairs |\n| --- | ---: " "| ---: |\n| Soundex | {} | {} |\n| native NYSIIS | {} | {} |\n",
               c.distinct_soundex, c.equal_soundex_pairs, c.distinct_nysiis,
               c.equal_nysiis_pairs);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(c.distinct_soundex),
                                      double(c.distinct_nysiis)},
                                     {"Soundex", "native NYSIIS"},
                                     "actual distinct keys");
    p.title("Original32-name cohort: descriptive grouping only").x_label(
        "native encoder").y_label("actual distinct key strings").save_svg(
        "build/nysiis_cohort.svg");
}
```
