> Make token and byte-policy differences visible

The controls AASCH andAEV expose whole-token behavior: replacing an internal SCH
withSS orEV withAF can retain repeated letters inside or across the token
boundary. LEW exposes the raw-predecessor W rule. Punctuation and an empty
string demonstrate the actual byte-domain contract, while a repeated long name
shows that no fixed output truncation is applied. These finite controls document
this native variant rather than asserting equality with a different library’s
algorithm.

Cleanup removes one trailingS when the key has more than one byte, folds a
trailingAY toY, then removes one trailingA if more than one byte remains. The
order matters, and the actual trace retains before/after states for each rule
even when no change occurs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nysiis_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nysiis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::string> inputs{"AASCH", "AEV", "LEW", "A-A", "",
                                    "MacDonaldMacDonald"}, labels{"SS token",
                                                                  "AF token",
                                                                  "raw W",
                                                                  "punctuation",
                                                                  "empty",
                                                                  "long key"};
    std::vector<double> lengths;
    std::print("| control | original bytes | actual native key | actual output bytes | actual interior " "tokens | whole tokens suppressed | actual capture units |\n| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); ++i) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::nysiis_trace(inputs[i]);
        lengths.push_back(t.analysis.key.size());
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | `{}` | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   inputs[i].empty() ? "(empty)" : inputs[i],
                   t.analysis.key.empty() ? "(empty)" : t.analysis.key,
                   t.analysis.key.size(), t.analysis.interior_tokens,
                   t.analysis.suppressed_tokens, t.captured_entries);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(lengths, labels, "actual key bytes");
    p.title("Native NYSIIS controls: tokens, raw bytes and no truncation").x_label("explicit input control").y_label("actual output bytes").save_svg("build/nysiis_controls.svg");
}
```
