\image(figures/nysiis_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual output sizes and token behavior of explicitly selected native-variant controls.)
\alttext(The computed table exposes internal token duplicates, raw-predecessor behavior, preserved punctuation, empty output and untruncated long keys.)

> Ownership, capture cost and references

Ordinary encoding is O(N) byte work and output/working storage, with safe
unsigned-byte C-library case conversion. It retains no caller references and
changes no locale; results depend on the process’s current C locale. Complete
byte strings, including embedded NUL or non-ASCII bytes, are accepted. This is
not Unicode phonetic normalization.

The owned trace retains original, uppercase, rewritten and final-key bytes. Each
actual decision additionally retains its stage/rule labels, full before/after
strings and token, plus one logical record unit. Every retained byte/record is
admitted before copying; default1000000 units and zero disables. Full
growing-key snapshots can cost O(N²), so trace size is not claimed linear merely
because ordinary encoding is linear. No partial trace is returned on quota
failure. Cohort comparison defaults to1000000 rows and uses balanced-map key
comparisons whose byte cost depends on key lengths.

[Apache Commons Codec NYSIIS documentation|https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-codec/apidocs/org/apache/commons/codec/language/Nysiis.html]
supplies context for a separate implementation, not an asserted oracle match.
The explicit native rule contract and actual histories are the authority for
this report. Descriptive group counts remain distinct from verified
pronunciation/identity accuracy or a universal superiority claim.

> Verification

This ten-report batch passes75 CTest cases,22 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,122 compiled and executed public examples,538/538 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python
arbitrary-precision arithmetic verifies69365 captured division records
with656460 checks; native independent polynomial, geometry, finite-range, graph,
ranking and callback checks cover the remaining producers. Frozen valid-input
comparisons preserve Neville recurrences, Newton result/callback paths, complete
byte encodings, switch routes and NSGA-II complete objective-call
sequences/final fronts. Ten checkout headers and ten byte-identical installed
development headers compile independently; an installed-header native consumer
links and runs. All40 complete programs execute, and40 native figures have been
visually reviewed; HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed rows/prose and
identical image bytes. Checks are scoped native checks, not an installation
claim for every language binding. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-254-263/`.
